  "Question": "Which of the following statements about sample representativeness is correct?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "As long as the sample is randomly selected from the population and its size is appropriate, it can reflect the population reasonably well",
    "B": "The larger the sample size, the more representative the sample must be, regardless of the selection method",
    "C": "Selecting only acquaintances makes the sample more convenient and more representative"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Representativeness depends on whether the selection method is random and whether the sample size is appropriate. When the sampling method is biased, even a large number of people does not necessarily make the sample representative.",
